# Vulnerabilities the Trivy scans (.github/workflows/security.yml) may let
# through. The scans fail only on HIGH or CRITICAL findings that already have a
# fix, so this should stay empty: update the base image or dependency instead.
#
# If one can't be fixed yet, or doesn't apply, add its id with an expiry and a
# comment saying why it is safe. On the expiry date it fails the build again, so
# nothing is waved through for good:
#
#   # spring-webmvc: fixed only in 7.0.11, which needs Boot 4.1.3
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
